## Stearic acid
component-stearic-acid = Stearic acid
    .genitive = stearic acid
component-stearic-acid-description-novice = A white waxy powder or lumps. It melts in hot water (at 69 °C); candles and soap are made of it.
component-stearic-acid-description-school = While molten stearic acid sets, it gives off latent heat and its temperature stays near 69 °C — the cooling graph shows a flat “shelf”.
component-stearic-acid-safety-school = The melt is hot (over 69 °C) — it can burn. Above 200 °C its vapour can catch fire.
